      "One ingredient, like Promix One Ingredient Whey",
      "NSF Contents Certified, per Naked",
      "Widely sold, including a 5 lb bag on Naked's site"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "About $2.10 per 25 g at the Amazon price we saw, more than Promix unflavored",
      "No lecithin, so it clumps more in a shaker",
      "Plain dairy taste, like any unflavored whey"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "Choose it over Promix if an outside certification matters more to you than the lower price.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein / serving": "25 g (Naked)",
      "Ingredients": "Grass-fed whey",
      "Third-party testing": "NSF Contents Certified (Naked)",
      "Cost per 25 g": "About $2.10 (Amazon price seen)"
    },
    "amazonUrl": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00XIKPUK4"
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: `${SITE_URL}/`,
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: `${SITE_URL}/best-of/`,
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Promix Protein Powder Review",
          item: `${SITE_URL}/promix-protein-powder-review/`,
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Promix protein powder third-party tested?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, by its own account. Promix says every product is third-party tested by Eurofins, and you can enter your bag's lot code on its lab results page to see the record. It publishes limits such as lead under 5 ppb. It does not claim NSF Certified for Sport, Informed Sport or Informed Choice, so it is not screened for banned substances in the way tested athletes need."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Promix protein powder healthy and clean?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Promix has some of the shortest labels in the category: two ingredients in the unflavored whey, one in One Ingredient Whey, and four in Vanilla Whey, with no gums, stevia or sucralose. Clean has no legal definition, though. The flavored bags add 4 to 5 g of sugar, and anyone with kidney disease, allergies or pregnancy should ask a doctor first."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Promix contain lactose?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Promix whey concentrate contains lactose, as all whey concentrates do, though Promix does not state the amount. Promix Whey Isolate is micro-filtered to under 1 g of lactose per serving, per Promix, which most people with lactose intolerance tolerate. Promix Vegan is dairy-free. Anyone with a milk allergy should avoid both wheys entirely, because the allergen is the milk protein itself."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Promix use stevia or artificial sweeteners?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Promix says its powders contain no stevia, sucralose or sugar alcohols. The unflavored whey, One Ingredient Whey and unflavored isolate are unsweetened. Vanilla Whey uses maple sugar, with 4 g added per serving, and the flavored isolates use organic coconut sugar, with 5 g added per serving, per Promix at the time of writing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which Promix flavor is best?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We have not tasted Promix, so we cannot rank flavors ourselves. Vanilla and chocolate are the core flavors across the whey, isolate and vegan lines, and the unflavored bags are the most versatile for cooking and smoothies. The isolate adds Cookies and Cream, Strawberry Milk and Banana Cream. Expect all of them to be less sweet than mainstream whey."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are the common complaints about Promix?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The predictable complaints follow from the label: unflavored Promix tastes like plain dairy, One Ingredient Whey needs a blender because it has no lecithin, and the flavored bags are milder than sucralose-sweetened shakes. Price is the other one. At about $1.73 to $2.14 per 25 g on Amazon, Promix costs more than mainstream whey blends."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Promix whey isolate better than Promix whey?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is better for lactose-sensitive buyers and anyone who wants more protein per scoop: 30 g against 25 g, with under 1 g of lactose, per Promix. It is worse on price, at about $2.11 per 25 g against about $1.73 for the unflavored concentrate at the Amazon prices we saw. If dairy suits you, the concentrate is the better buy."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: SITE_NAME, url: SITE_URL },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.brand ?? product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: author.name,
    section: "Brand Reviews",
    tags: [
      "promix protein powder",
      "promix whey protein powder",
      "promix whey isolate protein powder",
      "promix vegan protein",
      "promix review"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{
    text: "See Our Top Grass-Fed Whey Picks",
    link: "/best-grass-fed-whey-protein/",
  }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <ArticleHeader kicker={"Brand Review"} badge={"Label-Checked"} author={author} dates={dates} mobileAd={false}>
      <Fragment slot="title">Promix Protein Powder Review</Fragment>
      Promix whey, whey isolate and vegan protein checked by label: what is in each bag, how they are sweetened, what the Eurofins testing covers and what each costs per 25 g of protein.
    </ArticleHeader>

    <TableOfContents>
      <a href="#short-answer">Short Answer</a>
      <a href="#lineup">Product Lineup</a>
      <a href="#top-picks">The Products</a>
      <a href="#label">Label: Whey vs Isolate</a>
      <a href="#sweeteners">Sweeteners</a>
      <a href="#testing">Third-Party Testing</a>
      <a href="#cost">Cost per 25 g</a>
      <a href="#taste">Taste and Mixing</a>
      <a href="#vs">Promix vs Naked and Levels</a>
      <a href="#who">Who Should Buy</a>
      <a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </TableOfContents>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          Promix protein powder is a good buy for label readers: the whey has 25 g of grass-fed protein, the isolate 30 g, and none of it contains stevia or sucralose. What changes the verdict is price and certification, since Promix costs more than mainstream whey and relies on its own Eurofins testing. Below: every product, the label, the testing, cost per 25 g and alternatives.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Promix Protein Powder: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            Promix is a good grass-fed protein powder for people who read labels: its whey concentrate has 25 g of protein per serving, its whey isolate has 30 g, and the unflavored versions contain no sweetener at all. The flavored powders are sweetened with maple sugar or organic coconut sugar rather than stevia or sucralose, and Promix says every product is third-party tested by Eurofins. At the Amazon prices we saw, it costs about $1.73 per 25 g of protein for the unflavored whey and about $2.11 for the isolate.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Buy Promix if</strong> you want a short ingredient list, no non-nutritive sweeteners and a brand that publishes its heavy-metal specifications by lot. <strong>Skip it if</strong> you need a sport certification such as NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport, which Promix does not claim, or if price per gram is your main test, because big-tub wheys cost far less.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">Promix by the Numbers</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">25 g</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Protein per serving, Promix whey concentrate</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">30 g</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Protein per serving, Promix whey isolate</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">0 g</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Added sugar in the unflavored bags</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">$1.73</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Per 25 g, unflavored whey at the Amazon price we saw</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            This is a label-and-price review. We have not tasted Promix, so anything about taste and mixing is either Promix's own guidance or what the ingredient list predicts, and our approach is on our <a href="/how-we-test/">how we test</a> page. For Promix ranked against every other grass-fed whey, see our <a href="/best-grass-fed-whey-protein/">best grass-fed whey protein</a> guide.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="lineup" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. What Protein Powders Does Promix Sell?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Promix sells six kinds of protein powder: grass-fed whey concentrate, One Ingredient Whey, grass-fed whey isolate, a pea-based vegan protein, casein and a grass-fed beef protein isolate. All of them are listed on <a href="https://www.promixnutrition.com/">promixnutrition.com</a>, and most of the whey and vegan bags are also sold by Promix Nutrition on Amazon. The company was founded in 2011 by registered dietitian Albert Matheny, MS, RD, CSCS, per Promix, and is based in Gainesville, Florida.
          </p>

          <p>
            The whey concentrate is the core of the range. It comes in Unflavored, Vanilla, Raw Chocolate, Chocolate Peanut Butter and Cinnamon Swirl, all at $64 a bag on Promix's site at the time of writing. One Ingredient Whey is a separate listing at $64 for a 1 kg bag of 32 servings: the same grass-fed concentrate with nothing else added, not even the sunflower lecithin the regular unflavored bag uses.
          </p>

          <p>
            The whey isolate costs more, $76 a bag, and comes in six flavors: Unflavored, Vanilla, Chocolate, Cookies and Cream, Strawberry Milk and Banana Cream. The vegan protein is $58 a bag in Unflavored, French Vanilla and Raw Chocolate. Unflavored and Vanilla casein run $56 for 2.5 lb, and the beef protein isolate, in Unflavored, Creamy Vanilla and Rich Chocolate, is $64 for 30 servings with 30 g of protein each, per Promix.
          </p>

          <p>
            Promix also sells collagen peptides, protein puff bars, a co-branded Barry's Protein in whey and vegan versions, and a long list of non-protein supplements. This review sticks to the powders people search for as Promix protein powder, which in practice means the whey, the isolate and the vegan bags.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Promix powder</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Protein / serving</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Promix list price</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Flavors</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Whey (concentrate)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">25 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$64 per bag</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Unflavored, Vanilla, Raw Chocolate, Choc PB, Cinnamon Swirl</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">One Ingredient Whey</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">25 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$64 per 1 kg</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Unflavored only</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Whey Isolate</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30 to 31 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$76 per bag</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Unflavored, Vanilla, Chocolate, Cookies and Cream, Strawberry Milk, Banana Cream</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Vegan (pea isolate)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">25 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$58 per bag</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Unflavored, French Vanilla, Raw Chocolate</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Casein</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">25 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$56 per 2.5 lb</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Unflavored, Vanilla</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Beef Protein Isolate</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">$64 per 30 servings</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Unflavored, Vanilla, Chocolate</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. Promix Protein Powders Worth Buying, Plus One Alternative
          </h2>

          <p>
            Four Promix powders sold by Promix Nutrition on Amazon, and the grass-fed whey we would compare them with. Prices are what we saw on Amazon at the time of writing; label figures are per Promix and Naked.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <ProductCard product={product} rank={index + 1} />
          ))}
        </div>

        <div id="label" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. What Is in Promix Whey and Promix Whey Isolate?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Promix whey is a grass-fed whey protein concentrate with 25 g of protein per two-scoop serving, and Promix whey isolate is a grass-fed isolate with 30 g, per Promix at the time of writing. The unflavored concentrate has two ingredients, whey concentrate and non-GMO sunflower lecithin. One Ingredient Whey drops the lecithin. The isolate is micro-filtered to under 1 g of lactose per serving.
          </p>

          <p>
            One Ingredient Whey is the only plain Promix whey with its full panel printed in text on the product page: a 31 g serving gives 130 calories, 25 g of protein, 2 g of fat, 3 g of carbohydrate, 0 g of sugar and 110 mg of sodium, with 32 servings in the 1 kg bag. The regular unflavored whey lists 25 g of protein and 5.9 g of BCAAs; Promix does not print its calories in the page text, so check the label image on the listing if you count them.
          </p>

          <p>
            The flavored concentrate adds sugar but keeps the label short. Promix Vanilla Whey has four ingredients: grass-fed whey concentrate, North American maple sugar, whole bean Madagascar vanilla extract and sunflower lecithin. A 36 g serving gives 135 calories, 25 g of protein, 7 g of carbohydrate and 5 g of sugars, 4 g of them added. Raw Chocolate has 25 g of protein and 6.0 g of BCAAs and is described as lightly sweetened.
          </p>

          <p>
            The flavored isolates are sweetened only with organic coconut sugar. Per Promix's flavor table, Chocolate isolate gives 31 g of protein and 160 calories in a 44 g serving, and Vanilla isolate gives 30 g of protein and 150 calories in 38 g. Both carry 5 g of added sugar. Chocolate adds fair trade organic cocoa, Vanilla adds organic vanilla extractives, and both include under 1% sunflower lecithin.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Promix whey or Promix whey isolate?</h3>

          <p>
            Buy the isolate if lactose bothers you or you want the most protein per scoop; buy the concentrate if you tolerate dairy and want to save money. The isolate gives 5 g more protein per serving and less than 1 g of lactose, while the concentrate is cheaper per gram and keeps more of the milk fat. Promix says its concentrate is minimally filtered and contains omega-3s and CLA, though it does not publish the amounts. If you have a diagnosed milk allergy, neither is safe, because both are milk proteins; look at our <a href="/best-lactose-free-protein-powder/">lactose-free protein powder</a> picks or the vegan bag instead.
          </p>

