        <div id="taste" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            8. What Do Buyers Say About Promix Taste and Mixing?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Promix's product pages show a 4.9 average rating and hundreds of bags bought each month, but the honest summary from the label is simple: the unflavored powders taste like plain dairy and the flavored ones are only lightly sweet. We have not tasted Promix, so this section describes what the ingredients predict and what Promix itself tells buyers to expect.
          </p>

          <p>
            Unflavored Promix whey has no sweetener or flavor to mask the taste of milk protein, and Promix describes it as light and smooth rather than tasty. Most people who buy unflavored whey mix it into a smoothie, coffee, oatmeal or pancake batter rather than drinking it with water. One Ingredient Whey lacks even the sunflower lecithin that helps powder disperse, and Promix's own instructions say a blender or shaker bottle works best for it.
          </p>

          <p>
            The flavored powders are a different experience from a typical supermarket whey. Maple sugar and coconut sugar are far less sweet, gram for gram, than sucralose or stevia, so anyone used to a sucralose-sweetened shake should expect something milder. That is the point for buyers who chose Promix to get away from intense sweeteners, and a likely complaint for buyers who did not.
          </p>

          <p>
            For mixing, Promix recommends two scoops in 12 to 16 oz of water, milk or non-dairy milk, blended, shaken or stirred for about 30 seconds. Promix uses no gums, so shakes will be thinner than gum-thickened brands. If you want a thicker drink, blend with milk, a frozen banana or ice. The isolate dissolves more easily than the concentrate, which is typical of isolates in general.
          </p>

          <p>
            Flavor choice is the main gap. If you want a dessert-style whey with a long flavor list, the isolate's Cookies and Cream, Strawberry Milk and Banana Cream are Promix's closest answer, and our sibling review of <a href="/inno-supps-protein-powder-review/">Inno Supps Advanced Iso</a> covers a sweeter, more conventional isolate if that is what you are after.
          </p>
        </div>

