          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming grass-fed means certified</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Grass-fed on a Promix bag describes where the milk comes from, and Promix itself calls it a sourcing description rather than a certification. It says nothing about testing, purity or protein content. Judge Promix on its Eurofins lot testing and its label, and use our grass-fed guide to see how the claim varies between brands.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the isolate when the concentrate would do</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Promix Whey Isolate costs about $2.11 per 25 g at the Amazon price we saw, against about $1.73 for the unflavored concentrate. If dairy does not bother you, the extra 5 g of protein per scoop and the lower lactose are not worth roughly 22% more per gram of protein.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting a sucralose-sweet shake</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Promix's flavored powders use maple sugar or coconut sugar, which taste far milder than the sucralose or stevia most wheys use. Buyers switching from a mainstream brand can find the vanilla or chocolate underwhelming. Try a single bag first, or buy unflavored and sweeten it yourself.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating Eurofins testing as a sport certification</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Promix commissions its own testing from Eurofins and publishes the limits, which is useful. It is not NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport, the programs drug-tested athletes rely on to screen for banned substances. If you are tested, buy a certified product instead.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring servings when comparing bags</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Promix bags look identical, but servings differ: about 37 in the unflavored whey, 31 in Vanilla Whey and 26 in Chocolate isolate. Comparing on bag price alone hides those differences. Divide the price by the total protein in the bag to find the real cost per 25 g.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
